    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA most appealing end of terrace, two-story over garden level period property, enjoying impressive views across Dublin Bay to Howth and a west-facing rear garden, conveniently located a short walk to Sandymount Village and further enhanced by off street car parking to the rear. \n\nNo. 83 is a fine period property extending to approximately 183sqm. (1,969sq.ft.), laid out over three floors with separate access at the garden level. It enjoys huge scope and potential for the new owner to update and modernise to create a very special seafront family home with impressive views.\n\nThe property enjoys an ideal location on Strand Road close to the junction with Gilford Road which is within walking distance of Sandymount village and all its amenities including Sandymount Dart Station. The Merrion Shopping Centre and Blackrock village are also within easy access. Recreational amenities are well catered for in the area with the Railway Union cricket grounds, Westwood Leisure Complex and interesting beach walks adjacent."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHALL FLOOR - \n\n\nPorch - 1.85m x 1.8m\n\n\nReception Hall - 7.1m x 1.8m\nwith ceiling cornice work, inner arch.\n\nLiving Room - 4.85m x 4.6m\n(currently used as a bedroom), built in wardrobes either side of the bed, ceiling cornicing, timber sash window with commanding views over Sandymount Strand and Howth, sliding doors through to\n\nDining Room - 4.75m x 4m\nwith ceiling cornicing, painted marble fireplace with cast iron inset, timber sliding sash window.\n\nGARDEN LEVEL - \nwith own separate entrance.\n\nPorch - \nwith quarry tiled floor, opening into\n\nReception Hall - 1.85m x 7.8m\nwith quarry tiled floor.\n\nFamily Room - 4.7m x 4.6m\nwith wood burning stove set on a brick fireplace, arch through to the\n\nKitchen - 4m x 2.65m\nfitted with a range of presses, cupboards, drawers, worktop, one bowl stainless steel sink drainer unit, space for freestanding double oven with gas four ring hob, plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher, shelving, tiled floor, door out to the rear garden.\n\nShower Room - \nwith a corner shower unit with Mira electric shower, vanity wash hand basin with presses underneath, wc, wash hand basin, tiled floor, fully tiled walls.\n\nLobby Area - \nwith gas boiler, understairs storage, door out to the rear garden.\n\nFIRST FLOOR - \n\n\nHalf Landing - \nwith attractive fanlight and working shutters.\n\nLobby - \n\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.05m x 3.15m\nwith new timber double glazed sliding sash windows.\n\nShower Room - \ncomprising shower, wc, wash hand basin set into a tiled plinth.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.3m x 4.4m\nwith marble fireplace and raised brick hearth with an electric freestanding stove, arch leading through into\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.25m x 3.4m\nimpressive views across Dublin bay to Howth.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Appealing end of terrace, two-storey over garden level period property</li><li>Stunning sea views across Dublin Bay to Howth</li><li>West facing rear garden (approx. 19m. / 62ft.)</li><li>Off street car parking to the rear</li><li>Separate entrance at garden level</li><li>Highly convenient location</li><li>A short walk to Sandymount village</li><li>Gas fired central heating </li><li>Floor Area approx. 183sqm. (1,969sq.ft.)</ul>"
      },
